A||||9||lowfunds||87 vs 88||||1||
Z||000000||lowfunds||12-03-2000||12:15 PM||||Is a 88 worth getting over a 87 for an engine conversion? Is the lack of parts and high price for the 88 suspension worth the handling difference? Can the beretta brakes be used on the 88? I don't think they can. Thanks for any info...||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||12-03-2000||12:58 PM|||| The brakes are already upgraded on the '88s so you shouldn't worry about having to upgrade to GA/Beretta hardware.  I've only driven an '88 (GT) once.  I think I could tell a difference in the handling, but personally I wouldn't pay the extra money.  You can always spend the extra cash and upgrade an earlier year to match or even improve upon an '88 for the same or less money.  Just my opinion.  You're free to do what you want.  Just remember that any vehicle that old will have worn out suspention parts that you'll probably need to either replace or upgrade.||||reg||1
Z||000002||BAM-BAM||12-03-2000||01:22 PM||||   Go with the 87, the 88's are more expensive and the handling isn't all that compared to what you can do for less with the 87. Remember though, regardless of the year, parts are sometimes extremely hard to find, but with the earlier models, availability is greater do to greater production numbers and idiot drivers. You will become intimately familiar with your local wrecking yards for parts service. <P> Peace, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach/KYB Susp.<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats,headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Gauges And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||12-03-2000||01:26 PM||||I owned an 87 fiero coupe and now own an 88 formula coupe. The 87 coupe was fun to drive but it does not compare to the 88 in any way even with the rear sway bar and front Grand Am brakes I added to the coupe. The difference between the two is that the 88 rides allot better (even with the WS6 suspension), is easier to control when cornering at its limit, does not have the quirky handling characteristics associated with the 84-87 fiero's, has no bump steer, and stops better and shorter.<P>The Grand Am brakes are a good modification for the fiero but they are made of cast iron and are considerably heavier than the small aluminum calipers of the 88 or 87 models (more unsprung weight). I know because I installed them on my brothers 87 fiero. <P>I would recommend that you give up the Chevette and Citation based commuter car and get the only fiero I consider worth getting if you don't want to spend $$$$ in suspension modifications. The parts are not that hard to find and are only a little more expensive for some of the parts than the 84-87 model years. If you want the best handling, best riding, rarest, and most reliable fiero than get the 88-model year. <P><BR>I bet I get flamed for saying that!||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||12-03-2000||01:48 PM||||If quality (ride/handling)is your only concern, yes, I'd get an 88 in a second. <P>If ease/cost of ownership is a concern, then I'd avoid the 88's. Of all I've driven, the difference in handling and ride is marginal (but noticable), but not enough to suffer through the pain of finding suspension parts.  <P>Everyone's comments about the improvements are true, but keeping them in top shape costs more. <P>Can someone tell me one part in the Fiero rear suspension that is the same part number as a Citation (except bolts/nuts)? <P>Cradle? No. <BR>Control arms? No. <BR>Axles? No. <BR>Struts? No. <BR>Coils? No. <BR>Brakes? No.<BR>Bushings? Control arm and rear cradle maybe.<BR>Swaybar? None.<BR>Tie rods? No.<BR>Tie rod ends? Yep.<BR>Steering knuckle? No.<BR>Engine brackets/mounts? Maybe.<P>If it was the Citation front suspension, it would be far better. Other than being based on the GM FWD design, it's no more X body than it is A body or N body.<P><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 12-03-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||sqoach||12-03-2000||01:49 PM||||*dumps diesel on 88formula*<BR>*lights a match*<P>hehe<P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh<P>fiero7@hotmail.com||||reg||1
Z||000006||lowfunds||12-03-2000||05:46 PM||||Thanks for the info. Also as far as bump steer with the 87 vs 88 can the problem be corected on the 87? I have a 85SE and a 87GT now, and after I finish the 85 (stock rebuild) then Im doing the 3800SC install.Im just wondering if I should put it in the 87 or try to find a 88? Never driven a hopped up fiero so Im not sure how either would handle. I have always had 5.0s but,everyone and there brother has a 5.0 around here so I wanted somthing a little diffrent. Sorry for the rambling and thanks again for any advice.||||reg||1
Z||000007||My7Fieros||12-03-2000||06:46 PM||||Sqoach you ever dump gas on MY Formula and light a match it'll be BYE BYE time for you jack! ..................<BR>The 88s handle much better IMO..almost feels like power steering. Either/or would do just fine though.......||||reg||11
Z||000008||Black88GT||12-03-2000||07:22 PM||||The '88 Fiero has bump steer, just not as much.  The pre-88 bump steer is down right scary, especially on Baltimore City roads.  <P>I don't think ANY Fiero handles spectacularly on a bumpy road, however there is a big difference in the way they handle on those type of roads.  The '88 suspension feels more solid, I feel more confident in it.  <P>I am basing these opinions on driving an 86 GT with sway bar and KYBs vs. a stock Formula.<P>And BTW, '88 suspension parts are not hard to find, just pricey when you find them, which is the biggest factor with 95% of all Fiero owners.  I feel that is the reason why most don't want to own 88s, but thats IMHO of course...<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||terryk||12-03-2000||09:10 PM||||If think Black88GT said it better.<P>If I could get an 88 without people considering them equal to Ferrari's in cost, I wouldn't pass it up.||||reg||14
